# ADR-016: Move consultability from external set to VerificationFailure field

## Status

Accepted

## Context

Each verification rule produced a VerificationFailure with only
`rule` and `reason`. The classification "is this failure consultable
(LLM can retry via consult_procurement) or hard (terminate the run)"
lived in a separate frozenset, CONSULTABLE_RULES, in core/failures.py.
The Coordinator inspected `failure.rule in CONSULTABLE_RULES` at
runtime.

This separation created three problems. Adding a new rule required
edits in two places. The classification was not visible at the
construction site, only at routing time. Tools that produced their
own failures (after the Tool-Lifecycle refactor) would need to
import the global set.

## Decision

Add a `consultable: bool` field to VerificationFailure. Every rule
function and every inline failure construction sets the field at
the point of failure creation. The Coordinator routes by reading
`failure.consultable`.

## Consequences

Positive: classification lives next to the failure data. A reader
of any check_xxx function sees immediately whether the rule is
consultable. The Coordinator no longer imports a classification
table. Tools can construct failures without importing global sets.

Negative: every existing VerificationFailure construction had to be
updated to include the new keyword argument. The migration touched
all check_xxx functions plus the four inline constructions in
pipeline.py.

## Alternatives considered

Enum-typed FailureKind with values HARD and CONSULTABLE was
considered. Rejected because the two-value distinction is currently
boolean-shaped and an enum would add ceremony without payoff. If a
third category emerges, this decision is reversible in one
migration.